FILE: app/src/turntable.ts
```ts
import type { ArcRotateCamera, SceneContext } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { interpolateArcRotateCamera } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function spinAround(camera: ArcRotateCamera, scene: SceneContext, turns: number): Promise<void> {
    const startAlpha = camera.alpha;
    const goalAlpha = startAlpha + 2 * Math.PI * turns;
    return interpolateArcRotateCamera(camera, scene, { alpha: goalAlpha });
}
```

I wrote `src/turntable.ts` which delegates to the library's `interpolateArcRotateCamera`, passing only an `alpha` goal of `startAlpha + 2π·turns` so that beta, radius, and target are untouched and the library's exponential easing glides the camera the full unwrapped distance in the direction of increasing alpha. I was not sure whether `interpolateArcRotateCamera` is exported from the package root (`@babylonjs/lite`) or only from a sub-path, since the d.ts I was given is a flat concatenation of module files without a top-level `index.d.ts` to confirm the re-export; if the import fails, the correct specifier would be something like `@babylonjs/lite/camera/arc-rotate-interpolate`.
